<%# THE COLLECTION GRID — every seeded species, dex order, each drawn in its
    collection state: caught in full color, seen dimmed, unseen a silhouette. It is
    the same Seen/Caught numbers the cards above report, laid out as the dex being
    filled in rather than two totals.

    Every cell reads off PokemonPokedex#dex_entries, which projects the memos the
    cards already built — so all 251 cells cost ZERO extra queries. %>
<section class="card p-5" data-test="dex-grid">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 flex-wrap mb-5">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-heading">Collection</h2>

    <%# The legend. The artwork treatments carry the meaning, so they need a key — and
        each count is the number of CELLS wearing that treatment, which is why the
        middle chip is "Seen only" and not "Seen": the card above counts every species
        encountered (124), of which the caught ones are a subset drawn in their own
        state, so only the REMAINDER wears the seen treatment. The three add up to the
        dex; labelling that remainder "Seen" would put two different numbers under the
        same word on one page. %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-xs text-muted" data-test="dex-legend">
      <% [["Caught", caught_count, "bg-primary"],
          ["Seen only", seen_count - caught_count, "bg-secondary opacity-50"],
          ["Not seen", entries.size - seen_count, "bg-inset border border-subtle"]].each do |label, count, swatch| %>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full <%= swatch %>"></span>
          <%= label %>
          <span class="text-secondary font-semibold tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(count) %></span>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-6 lg:grid-cols-8 xl:grid-cols-10 gap-3">
    <% entries.each do |entry| %>
      <%= render "dex_cell", entry: entry %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
